## 4. File Change Summary Tables

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/config/apps.js` | Create | `APPS`, `setPendingParams`, `getPendingParams` | Single registry defining every app: desktop component/key/params + mobile `route()`. |
| `src/views/AppRouteView.vue` | Create | `AppRouteView` | Generic route host; resolves component from `route.meta.app`, feeds params (pending → route fallback). |
| `src/router/index.ts` | Modify | `routes` | Added `/team` + one route per uncovered app (`wiki`, `docs`, `knowledge`, `knowledge-settings`, `profiles`, `projects`, `activity`, `settings`, `global-settings`, `account`, `file-explorer`, `file-viewer`, `logs`, `chat-logs`, `metrics`, `vibe-coding`, `team-channel`, `team-dm`, `team-media-library`). |
| `src/router/index.ts` | Modify | module tail | Added `$storex.$navigation = router.$navigation` (was referenced by the store but never assigned). |
| `src/router/navigate.js` | Modify | `openApp` (new) | Single panel-vs-route decision point + transient payload hand-off. |
| `src/router/navigate.js` | Modify | `chats/meets/workspaces/browsers/apps` | All openers funnel through `openApp`; fixed bogus `/files`,`/wiki`,`/team` pushes that hit the catch-all. |
| `src/store/ui.js` | Modify | `mutations.setActiveTab` | On mobile, delegates to `openApp` (so every `setActiveTab` launcher works on mobile); desktop branch unchanged. |
| `src/store/ui.js` | Modify | `openChat`, `openFileInViewer`, `toggleLogs`, `openChatLogs` | Mutations now delegate to `openApp`. |
| `src/store/ui.js` | Modify | actions | Added `openApp`; refactored `openTeamChannel/DM/MediaLibrary`, `openVibeCoding/Projects/Teams/Workspaces/Workspace/Meet/Planning/Tutorial` to `openApp`. |

**How to open an app now — one way:**

```js
// Components / stores
$storex.ui.openApp('wiki')                               // panel (desktop) | route (mobile)
$storex.ui.openApp('chat', { chat })                     // chat panel | /chats/:id/:name
$storex.ui.openApp('team-dm', { team, member, chatId })  // panel | /team-dm/:id
$storex.ui.setActiveTab('profiles')                      // launchers keep working everywhere
```

**⚠️ One decision to confirm:** the split predicate is `$storex.ui.isMobile`. The old `openChat` used `isDesktopMode` (route name `codx-junior-split`). If your desktop layout can sit on a non‑`/desktop` route and still show panels, we should switch the predicate to `$storex.ui.isDesktopMode` — it's a one‑line change inside `openApp`.

**Known follow-ups (not changed to avoid unrelated risk):**
- `openMediaLibrary` / `'media-library'` has no component or route (pre-existing; left as-is).
- Team‑sub‑objects (`team`, `member`, `channel`) rely on the transient payload on hard refresh; if you need refresh‑proof deep links, add a small store resolver in `apps.js` (`resolveParams(route, $storex)`).
- Existing saved layouts are unaffected — desktop dedup keys are preserved.

